      "source_review": [
        "Independent cached PCI activation and per-function allocation failure; exact family unregister, callback-ID revalidation and instance IRQ cookies.",
        "Atomic HID identity check, exact per-device class binding and requested PCI note lifetime; separate MSC storage lanes.",
        "Runtime attach uses existing storage gate, device-use lease and mount publisher. Offline close denies new I/O, while exact already-pinned work can drain.",
        "Mounted/active/uncertain registrations stay retained; only exact successful retirement permits media-entry reuse. Detailed contracts: KernelRustUsb.txt."
      ],
      "qualification_limits": [
        "Local KVM/SMP4 only, no native AMD/OssiPC or Windows run.",
        "One real emulated controller halt and failed read; no full PCI-loss, DMA/allocation-failure or interleaving matrix.",
        "Shared-INTx/unregister/pollfallback routing is source-reviewed; actual missing-IRQ injection remains for .28.",
        "Old mounts retain their original identity; no persistence acknowledgement or unconditional forced unmount after physical removal."
      ],
      "performance_claim": "Functional isolation; one normal STANDARD is a bounded regression observation, not a USB throughput improvement claim."
    },
